# Keep-delivered credentials: what scripts/keep/credential-health.sh checks, one per line.
# Keep (~/.keep on the owner's Mac) delivers each as /run/keep/<id>; a unit loads it by
# LoadCredential=<id>:/run/keep/<id>. Names, paths and URLs only: never a value here.
#
# Fields, separated by "|" (blanks around a field are ignored; "-" means none):
#   id              the Keep id: the file /run/keep/<id>, and the alert subject
#   unit            the systemd user unit that loads it (LoadCredential=<id>:...)
#   health_url      a URL the unit answers 200 on while up
#   status_tag      the prefix of the unit's journal status lines: "<tag>: <http code> ..."
#   legacy_file     the plaintext file Keep replaced (~ is the home directory): must stay gone
#   legacy_keys     the env names it had there (comma-separated): no spawn-* unit may set them
#   scanner_source  a plaintext file scripts/redact/secret-values.py reads it from (~ is the
#                   home directory): an alert when it is missing and /run/keep/<id> is too
#                   (then every value scan refuses). "-" for a credential whose plaintext is
#                   retired (its legacy_file): delivery_missing already says Keep's file is gone.
#
# id               | unit                    | health_url                     | status_tag | legacy_file                  | legacy_keys      | scanner_source
typesafe.api-key   | spawn-jev-relay.service | http://127.0.0.1:8790/healthz  | jev-relay  | ~/.config/spawn/typesafe.env | TYPESAFE_API_KEY | -
